WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.834
-Welcome back, everybody.
We're talking to Bad Bunny!

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:05.968
Now, you're --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:09.667
You're releasing music maybe,
you're going on tour definitely,

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:11.167
and now you're making
your acting debut

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:13.868
in "Narcos: Mexico."
I mean --

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:16.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:18.167
You're used to performing.
You've done almost everything.

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:20.501
How different was this?

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:23.467
-It's different, but at the same
time, it's the same, you know?

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:27.367
You have to work hard
to be responsible

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:31.334
and, you know,
respect the colleagues.

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:33.467
-Yeah, of course.
-I enjoy.

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:35.534
You know,
it's something new for me,

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:37.467
but I like it, and I enjoy it.

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:40.400
I'm learning and practicing.
I keep practicing, you know?

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.334
-Did you go to them,
or did they come to you?

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:47.200
-They come to me.
-Of course.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.834
As I figured, yeah.
But I don't know

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:52.234
if you were a fan of --
I mean, if you're a fan of --

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:53.934
'Cause I love "Narcos."
I've seen it, I go --

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:55.367
-No, me too.
Me too.

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:57.601
-Can you set up your character
and who you play?

00:00:57.601 --> 00:01:01.334
-My character is Benito --
I'm Kitty Páez.

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:02.400
Kitty Páez.
-Kitty?

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.400
-Kitty.
-Yep.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.067
-Kitty Páez.
-Gotta love it, man.

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:06.901
-Yeah.
-Yeah, that's good.

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:11.000
-Yeah, he's a member of the
Arellano-Félix organization.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.634
They have the cartel in Tijuana.
-Yeah.

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:17.367
-And he's one of the --

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:20.033
-He's one of the new young kids
that are like --

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:22.234
-Yeah.
-Not old school.

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:25.334
Like, you guys are, like,
going to clubs and stuff

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.300
and doing stuff
you shouldn't be doing.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.434
-He's part of the -- one of the
Narco Juniors, the young guys.

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:34.200
-Also, you're such a nice,
positive guy.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.133
Is it tough to act
and be this mean?

00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:39.767
-I'm a good guy.
-You're a Bad Bunny,

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.033
but you're a good man,
yeah, absolutely.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:45.267
-But it was fun.
You know, it was fun.

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:51.000
And the character is, like,
a cool guy, young guy.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.501
I'm a cool guy, I think so,
I don't know.

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:54.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.167
-You're one of the coolest, man.
I just love that you did it.

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:57.701
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Bad Bunny

00:01:57.701 --> 00:02:01.701
in "Narcos: Mexico" this Friday.
Take a look.

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.701
[ Conversing in Spanish ]

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.400
-That's my man, Bad Bunny!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.667
The third season
of "Narcos: Mexico"

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:53.467
begins streaming this Friday
on Netflix!

